+
+## Conventions
+
+### Command prefix aliasing
+
+Slash commands in this repo always use the canonical `geno-` prefix in source (e.g., `/geno-mine-extract`). When installed via `geno-tools`, the installer may configure shorter aliases depending on the user's `~/.geno/config.yaml` `aliases.command_prefix` setting. Always author skill names and docs with the canonical `geno-` prefix; alias mapping is handled at install time and never committed to this repo.
+
+### Adding a new skill
+
+1. Create a directory under `skills/` named after the skill (e.g., `skills/geno-mine-<verb>/`).
+2. Add a `SKILL.md` with YAML frontmatter (`name`, `description`, `allowed-tools`, `argument-hint`, `license`, `metadata`).
+3. Add a row to the Skills table in this file.
+4. If the skill has a corresponding CLI subcommand, add it in `geno_mine/cli.py`.
+
+### Versioning
+
+The canonical version lives in `genotools.yaml` (`version` field). Keep `pyproject.toml` (`project.version`) in sync. Bump the version when skills are added, removed, or behavior changes.
